  {
   "method_name": "Diffusion-QL",
   "is_own_method": true,
   "one_paragraph_description": "Diffusion-QL represents the policy as an MLP-based conditional diffusion model over actions given state: an action is produced at runtime by running N reverse denoising steps from Gaussian noise conditioned on the state. Training minimizes a behavior-cloning diffusion loss Ld (regularizing toward the dataset actions) plus a Q-learning term Lq that maximizes Q of the sampled action, weighted by alpha = eta / E|Q|, with gradients backpropagated through the whole diffusion chain; two Q-networks with target networks and double-Q (clipped min) are learned via the Bellman objective (Algorithm 1).",
   "conventional_lineage_hint": "offline RL, policy-regularization family: 'Offline reinforcement learning (RL), which aims to learn an optimal policy using previously collected static datasets' ; 'we analyze why Diffusion-QL outperforms the other policy-constraint based methods'",
